# JustAC local pin: upstream ships no SimulationCraft list for this spec. A Mistweaver
# damage priority for the gaps between heals, grounded at client build 12.1.0.69875:
# Rising Sun Kick (Rushing Wind Kick when talented) on cooldown, Blackout Kick spending
# every Teachings of the Monastery window (one Tiger Palm, one Blackout Kick, for the most
# Rising Sun Kick resets), the Jade Empowerment charges, Spinning Crane Kick at three or more
# targets. A Dance of Chi-Ji proc and the out-of-range Crackling Jade Lightning are left to
# Assisted Combat, which sees both; ranked here they could only read as "always" (an
# unconditional lightning line would also erase the Jade Empowerment gate).
# Celestial Conduit (Conduit of the Celestials) is a damage button too; Master of Harmony
# adds no button of its own. Thunder Focus Tea, the celestial invokes and Sheilun's Gift
# are healing and never reach the damage queue. Anything the character does not know is
# dropped at runtime.

actions=touch_of_death
actions+=/celestial_conduit
actions+=/rising_sun_kick
# The empowered charges never expire, so they wait behind Rising Sun Kick. A stack gate,
# not .up, so the line is checked wherever the aura can be read.
actions+=/crackling_jade_lightning,if=talent.jade_empowerment&buff.jade_empowerment.stack>=1
actions+=/blackout_kick,if=buff.teachings_of_the_monastery.stack>=1
# Assisted Combat waits for four targets; the AoE tier here covers three and up, and big
# pulls are where Spinning Crane Kick earns its place over Tiger Palm.
actions+=/spinning_crane_kick,if=active_enemies>=3
actions+=/tiger_palm
